-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 17: JUDGMENTS AND ORDERS (roc3, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or `MAYBE NUMBER`).
--   JUST TRUE / a number   the text says yes (or gives the figure) on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE             the text says no in its own words: a flat negative, a period it fixes
--                          in its own words that has run out, an "if", "where" or "unless" that
--                          is met or not met as the words say, or a definition that says "means".
--   NOTHING                the text does not answer: it limits a grant by its own wording (a scope
--                          with no "only", a manner, a complement), or is silent, or points outside.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A question whose answer is a number cannot say JUST FALSE; where the text's "where" is not met
-- it answers NOTHING, and the comment says so (a fork recorded in NOTES.md).
-- TIME.  A period is a constant of the core type `Period`; whether an act is in time is decided
-- against the input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (PLAN.md 5.1, S-T1).

