§§ `Rule 1 -- definition of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1671 | 1. In this Order, “order” means an order of the Court and includes a judgment given at any stage of the action, whether after trial or hearing or otherwise.
@ref O 17 r 1 (src:1671)
GIVEN `the thing is an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a judgment given at any stage of the action, whether after trial or hearing or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 17 r 1 the thing is an order for the purposes of this Order` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a judgment given at any stage of the action, whether after trial or hearing or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- includes: "includes a judgment given at any stage of the action, whether after trial or hearing or otherwise"
    ELSE
        IF `the thing is an order of the Court`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- means: "“order” means an order of the Court"
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“order” means an order of the Court and includes a judgment given at any stage of the action" (a definition that says "means"; the list of the two limbs is read as closed)

