§§ `Rule 4 -- redaction and prohibition of inspection or copying of orders`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1685 | 4. —(1) The Court may redact any order in the interests of justice or where the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law. (2) The Court may prohibit any person, other than the parties, from inspecting or taking copies of any order in the interests of justice or where the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law.
@ref O 17 r 4(1) (src:1685)
GIVEN `redaction is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 17 r 4(1) the Court may redact the order` MEANS
    IF `redaction is in the interests of justice` OR `the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the interests of justice or where the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

@ref O 17 r 4(2) (src:1685)
GIVEN `the person is a party to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prohibition is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 17 r 4(2) the Court may prohibit the person from inspecting or taking copies of the order` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party to the action`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person, other than the parties"
    ELSE
        IF `prohibition is in the interests of justice` OR `the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the interests of justice or where the order was made in hearings which were conducted in private under any written law" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

